* ---- sim/vco-bias-current/testbench/tb_vco_bias.spice (sha256 1f8652736b5893c47711e7ad58750dd806b2bb56391e76ccdb6838042ad41b91)
* gf180-pll :: vco-bias-current :: constant-gm reference current of the VCO bias
* generator, as specified (ppolyf_u_3k) vs. as the pre-#381 layout drew it
*
* sim/harness netlist FRAGMENT (see sim/harness/README.md). Two DUTs are
* composed ahead of this file by the manifest's `dut` key and are never copied
* into it:
*   - design/netlist/vco.spice                          -> .subckt vco_bias
*   - .../vco_bias_as_drawn_350.spice (generated)       -> .subckt vco_bias_as_drawn_350
*
* WHAT THIS DECK MEASURES AND WHY
* -------------------------------
* `design/netlist/vco.spice` declares RCG/ROFF/RDEG as `ppolyf_u_3k`
* (3000 ohm/sq). Until issue #381 the layout generator drew them as the
* unmarked `ppolyf_u` class (350 ohm/sq) at the same W/L -- an 8.6x
* sheet-resistance error sitting directly on RCG, which sets the
* beta-multiplier (constant-gm) reference current. This deck measures the
* consequence rather than asserting it: both bias generators are instantiated
* side by side at the same PVT point, from the same rails, and their currents
* are compared.
*
* Three quantities per arm, at each of three control voltages:
*
*   i_bias   total current drawn from vdd_vco by the bias generator itself.
*   i_tail   drain current of a REPLICA of vco_stage.sch's own tail device
*            (MNT: nfet_03v3 W=4 um L=0.5 um, gate on VBN), its drain held at
*            mid-rail. This is the per-stage starving current the 5-stage ring
*            is biased to, i.e. the quantity f_osc is proportional to -- read
*            off a replica rather than the ring itself so the measurement is a
*            fast DC operating point with no oscillator in the deck.
*   i_head   the same for the stage's head device (MPH: pfet_03v3 W=10 um
*            L=0.5 um, gate on VBP, source on vdd_vco).
*
* The replicas carry the identical geometry parameters vco_stage.sch gives
* those two devices (ad/as/pd/ps/nrd/nrs expressions included verbatim), so
* they are the schematic's devices held at a DC bias, not a re-sizing.
*
* Four witness resistors (both classes, both drawn lengths, 1.0 V across each)
* measure the sheet resistance the corner actually delivers, so the record
* states the resistance behind every current it reports instead of quoting a
* model parameter. i(v...) of those sources is negative by SPICE convention;
* the manifest's measure expressions negate it.
*
* The ring, the output buffer and the 22 pF decap pair are deliberately NOT in
* this deck: the claim under test is the bias generator's own operating point,
* and leaving `cap_nmos_03v3` out also keeps the deck runnable on either
* ngspice-46 or -47 (see sim/harness/README.md's nonlinear-moscap note).
*
* From the harness: vdd_val, vdd_nom, temp_c.
* From the manifest's `band` sweep axis: b0, b1, b2.

* --- control voltages: bottom, middle and top of the usable Vctrl window
* (0.9 .. 2.7 V, DR-001 Decision 3 / spec/pll.md's tuning-range section).
.param vc_lo=0.9 vc_mid=1.8 vc_hi=2.7

* --- rails and static band-select code -------------------------------------
vdd vdd 0 dc {vdd_val}
vb0 b0 0 dc {b0 * vdd_val}
vb1 b1 0 dc {b1 * vdd_val}
vb2 b2 0 dc {b2 * vdd_val}

vctl_lo  vc_lo  0 dc {vc_lo}
vctl_mid vc_mid 0 dc {vc_mid}
vctl_hi  vc_hi  0 dc {vc_hi}

* --- arm A: as specified (ppolyf_u_3k, 3000 ohm/sq) -------------------------
vam_a_lo  vdd a_lo_vdd  dc 0
xa_lo  vc_lo  b0 b1 b2 a_lo_vbp  a_lo_vbn  a_lo_vdd  0 vco_bias
vam_a_mid vdd a_mid_vdd dc 0
xa_mid vc_mid b0 b1 b2 a_mid_vbp a_mid_vbn a_mid_vdd 0 vco_bias
vam_a_hi  vdd a_hi_vdd  dc 0
xa_hi  vc_hi  b0 b1 b2 a_hi_vbp  a_hi_vbn  a_hi_vdd  0 vco_bias

* --- arm B: as the pre-#381 layout drew it (ppolyf_u, 350 ohm/sq) -----------
vam_b_lo  vdd b_lo_vdd  dc 0
xb_lo  vc_lo  b0 b1 b2 b_lo_vbp  b_lo_vbn  b_lo_vdd  0 vco_bias_as_drawn_350
vam_b_mid vdd b_mid_vdd dc 0
xb_mid vc_mid b0 b1 b2 b_mid_vbp b_mid_vbn b_mid_vdd 0 vco_bias_as_drawn_350
vam_b_hi  vdd b_hi_vdd  dc 0
xb_hi  vc_hi  b0 b1 b2 b_hi_vbp  b_hi_vbn  b_hi_vdd  0 vco_bias_as_drawn_350

* --- the 100 MHz reference point, hardwired (NOT on the band sweep axis) ----
* spec/pll.md's power section names "100 MHz (band 5, Vctrl 1.8 V)" as the
* reference operating point its ratified 318 uA `vdd_vco` domain current is
* measured at, so the one absolute, spec-anchored check in this campaign needs
* that point present at EVERY grid point rather than only on the band-sweep
* slice that happens to select it. B2 B1 B0 = 101.
vb5_0 b5_0 0 dc {vdd_val}
vb5_1 b5_1 0 dc 0
vb5_2 b5_2 0 dc {vdd_val}

vam_a_b5 vdd a_b5_vdd dc 0
xa_b5 vc_mid b5_0 b5_1 b5_2 a_b5_vbp a_b5_vbn a_b5_vdd 0 vco_bias
vam_b_b5 vdd b_b5_vdd dc 0
xb_b5 vc_mid b5_0 b5_1 b5_2 b_b5_vbp b_b5_vbn b_b5_vdd 0 vco_bias_as_drawn_350

* --- ring-stage replica probes ----------------------------------------------
* One MNT (tail) + one MPH (head) per arm per control voltage, drain/source
* held at mid-rail through a 0 V-offset source that doubles as the ammeter.
.param vmid='vdd_val/2'

vnt_a_lo  a_lo_nt  0 dc {vmid}
xnt_a_lo  a_lo_nt  a_lo_vbn  0 0 nfet_03v3 L=0.5u W=4u nf=1 ad='int((nf+1)/2) * W/nf * 0.18u' as='int((nf+2)/2) * W/nf * 0.18u' pd='2*int((nf+1)/2) * (W/nf + 0.18u)'
